{"id": "EUVD-2026-107385", "enisaUuid": "46ac377b-238d-3a07-80e5-a460f73f6b9b", "description": "Multiple Cisco products are affected by a vulnerability in the Snort 3 Detection Engine that could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause the detection engine to unexpectedly restart, resulting in a denial of service (DoS) condition.\r\n\r\nThe vulnerability is due to a flaw in logic handling when General Packet Radio Service (GPRS) Tunneling Protocol (GTP) extension headers are processed within the codec. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted, fragmented UDP datagram that contains these headers to the Snort 3 Detection Engine of an affected device. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to cause the detection engine to enter an infinite loop, resulting in a DoS condition.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T16:14:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T19:11:11", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L", "references": ["https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-snort3-gtpcodec-dos-Rmecfepz"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-76445", "GHSA-5cgp-9338-jh6r"], "assigner": "cisco", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0053b2fc-cade-30c9-b0b5-368dd113879e", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.3.1.0"}, {"id": "01b82757-5af2-3b3e-9e79-8c4b1aff4562", "product": {"name": "Cisco UTD SNORT IPS Engine Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "17.18.1"}, {"id": "027dbbd3-7f92-3b2b-9476-6d8965a36835", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Threat Defense (FTD) Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "7.2.6"}, {"id": "033ba77c-b0b4-3809-954c-45d777d242a5", "product": {"name": "Cisco UTD SNORT IPS Engine Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "17.15.4"}, {"id": "0658fe11-0c8e-3259-b2ac-10bfedc4a651", "product": {"name": "C